│ patch_name               │ parametrized_chain_with_sharing                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the fixed CZ chain in the current program with parametrized CRX gates using       │
│                          │ parameter sharing. The current program achieves good accuracy (0.89 validation) but       │
│                          │ suffers from very slow convergence (750 steps). The prior program with parametrized CRZ   │
│                          │ gates converged much faster (150 steps).                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key insight is that parametrized gates enable faster learning, but we can keep        │
│                          │ parameter efficiency by reusing the same parameter across multiple gates in a pattern.    │
│                          │ This combines:                                                                            │
│                          │ - The fast convergence of parametrized gates (program 1)                                  │
│                          │ - The structured chain topology that worked well in the current program                   │
│                          │ - Aggressive parameter sharing to keep the parameter count reasonable                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ We'll use CRX gates (control-rotation-X) with a repeating pattern of 3 shared parameters, │
│                          │ creating a learnable entangling structure that's more efficient than fixed gates but      │
│                          │ simpler than fully independent parameters.                                                │
