╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ layered_alternating_entanglement                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ This novel approach draws inspiration from both prior programs but implements a           │
│                          │ fundamentally different architectural strategy.                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key insights from prior programs:                                                         │
│                          │ 1. Program 1 used per-qubit parameters (146 params) but achieved good accuracy (0.88      │
│                          │ test) with high convergence steps (330).                                                  │
│                          │ 2. Program 2 achieved excellent parameter efficiency (38 params) with minimal             │
│                          │ generalization gap (0.01) and fast convergence (180 steps), suggesting aggressive         │
│                          │ parameter sharing is beneficial.                                                          │
│                          │ 3. Current program uses 74 params with moderate performance.                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Novel approach: **Layered Alternating Entanglement with Adaptive Parameter Reuse**        │
│                          │ - Replace the star/hub topology with a **layered alternating pattern** that cycles        │
│                          │ between different entanglement schemes across multiple layers.                            │
│                          │ - Use **three layers** of increasingly sparse entanglement rather than a single dense     │
│                          │ layer, allowing parameter copies to appear at different circuit depths.                   │
│                          │ - Implement **selective parameter reuse** where certain parameters are reused across      │
│                          │ different layers but in different contexts (different qubit pairs).                       │
│                          │ - Combine fixed CZ gates (layer 1) with parametrized CRY gates (layer 2) with fixed CNOT  │
│                          │ gates (layer 3) for diversity.                                                            │
│                          │ - Reduce post-entanglement parameters by using shared parameters across the final layers. │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This differs from prior approaches by:                                                    │
│                          │ - Not using simple even/odd sharing (Program 2 weakness: too rigid)                       │
│                          │ - Not using per-qubit parameters (Program 1 weakness: too many parameters)                │
│                          │ - Using structured multi-layer entanglement that balances expressivity and efficiency     │
│                          │ - Convergence expected around 220-250 steps with better generalization                    │
