│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ minimal_hybrid_ansatz                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves a good balance but shows room for improvement in validation  │
│                          │ accuracy (0.87) and has some overfitting (generalization_gap: 0.04). The prior programs   │
│                          │ reveal two key insights:                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Seed 1** (0.87 score): Uses minimal parameters (38) with aggressive sharing (only 2  │
│                          │ unique params in RY, 2 in each RZ layer), achieving excellent parameter efficiency but    │
│                          │ lower overall accuracy (0.86).                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Seed 2** (0.87 score): Uses more parameters (86) with parametrized two-qubit gates   │
│                          │ (CRY), achieving higher training accuracy (0.94) but worse generalization and slower      │
│                          │ convergence.                                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current program (74 params, 0.87 score) sits between these two approaches. To         │
│                          │ improve, I propose a **hybrid minimal architecture** that:                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ - Returns to aggressive parameter sharing like Seed 1 (reduce to ~40 params)              │
│                          │ - Adds a single global RX rotation per qubit at the end as recommended                    │
│                          │ - Simplifies the entanglement structure to use a pure nearest-neighbor chain (more        │
│                          │ device-friendly, faster convergence)                                                      │
│                          │ - Eliminates skip-links and redundant layers that increased complexity without            │
│                          │ proportional gains                                                                        │
│                          │ - Maintains the paired sharing pattern which showed robustness                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This approach prioritizes **convergence speed** (currently 150 steps), **parameter        │
│                          │ efficiency**, and **reduced generalization gap** while leveraging the proven              │
│                          │ minimal-sharing pattern that achieved excellent validation accuracy in Seed 1.            │
