│ patch_description        │ This redesigned program extends the highly-efficient current architecture by introducing  │
│                          │ a second structured RY layer with orthogonal grouping after the post-entanglement RZ      │
│                          │ block. While the initial RY and RZ layers use even/odd pairing (qubits [0,2,4,6]→"a" and  │
│                          │ [1,3,5,7]→"b"), the new final RY layer uses cross-paired grouping (qubits                 │
│                          │ [0,2,4,6]→"ry_final_c" and [1,3,5,7]→"ry_final_d"). This captures rotational modes missed │
│                          │ by the single even/odd pattern, enriching local expressivity without bloating the         │
│                          │ parameter count. The new layer adds only 2 parameters while preserving the fast           │
│                          │ convergence (180 steps) and minimal generalization gap achieved by aggressive parameter   │
│                          │ sharing. Total parameters increase from 50 to 52, maintaining parameter efficiency while  │
│                          │ improving expressivity through structural diversity.                                      │
