                         Patch Metadata - Gen 19/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ merge_rz_parameters                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ The current program has a score of 0.87 with 74 parameters and a significant              │
│                          │ generalization gap (0.04). The prior best program (score 0.91) achieved better accuracy   │
│                          │ with only 44 parameters by removing redundant parametrization.                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key insight is that the current program separates pre- and post-entanglement RZ       │
│                          │ rotations into distinct parameters (rz_pre_a/b/c/d and rz_post_a/b/c/d), doubling the RZ  │
│                          │ parameter count to 8 per group. However, both layers serve the same role—local phase      │
│                          │ adjustment before and after entanglement.                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The recommendation is to merge these by using a single shared RZ parameter per qubit      │
│                          │ group (rz_a, rz_b, rz_c, rz_d) instead of separate pre/post versions. Each qubit will     │
│                          │ still receive two RZ rotations (maintaining expressivity), but they will share the same   │
│                          │ angle. This:                                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Reduces n_params from 74 to 40 (by 46%), improving parameter efficiency                │
