│ patch_description        │ The current program (0.87 score) has overfit with 86 parameters and poor generalization   │
│                          │ (gap 0.06). The prior best (0.91 score) used only 44 parameters with excellent            │
│                          │ generalization (gap 0.01) and achieved convergence in 180 steps vs 540 for current.       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The prior best structure is proven: initial RY → pre-RZ (2 params) → linear CZ chain →    │
│                          │ reverse CRZ chain → post-RZ (2 params).                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit replaces the reverse CRZ chain with CRY gates. Both use the same 1 shared       │
│                          │ parameter per layer, maintaining the 44-parameter budget. However, CRY (rotation around   │
│                          │ Y-axis) may provide better complementarity to the forward CZ chain than CRZ (controlled   │
│                          │ phase). This trades CRZ's phase control for CRY's amplitude modulation while keeping the  │
│                          │ architecture minimal and parameter-efficient.                                             │
