│ patch_name               │ split_crz_reverse_chain                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ The prior best candidate (score 0.91) achieved strong performance with a parametrized     │
│                          │ reverse CRZ chain using a single shared parameter. The current candidate (score 0.88)     │
│                          │ replaced this with fixed CZ gates and added a global RX layer, which decreased accuracy.  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit restores the parametrized reverse CRZ chain but splits it into two              │
│                          │ complementary parameters:                                                                 │
│                          │ - "crz_rev_a": controls odd-indexed backward links (7→6, 5→4, 3→2, 1→0)                   │
│                          │ - "crz_rev_b": controls even-indexed backward links (6→5, 4→3, 2→1)                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This design doubles the entangling-angle variety with minimal parameter overhead (+1      │
│                          │ parameter vs. single shared parameter), allowing the circuit to probe richer correlations │
│                          │ between even and odd qubits while maintaining excellent parameter efficiency. The global  │
│                          │ RX layer is removed since it didn't improve performance and adds unnecessary overhead.    │
