│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ skip_link_cz_expressivity                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The prior programs show that a linear chain of CZ gates combined with reverse             │
│                          │ parametrized gates achieves strong performance (0.91 score). However, the current program │
│                          │ attempts to add global mixing layers, which increases parameters to 62 and degrades       │
│                          │ performance (0.90 score).                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key insight from the recommendation: augment the zero-cost CZ chain with skip-link CZs    │
│                          │ that connect non-adjacent qubits at no parameter cost. This broadens long-range           │
│                          │ connectivity without the parameter bloat seen in the current approach.                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Novel approach: Instead of adding more parametrized gates globally, strategically insert  │
│                          │ fixed CZ skip-links at mid-range qubit pairs (0–2, 2–4, 4–6, 6–0) to create a mesh-like   │
│                          │ topology. This maintains the efficient parameter count while enabling richer              │
│                          │ correlations. The skip-links act as shortcuts through the linear chain, promoting         │
│                          │ information flow and nonlocal entanglement patterns that the reverse parametrized layer   │
│                          │ can exploit.                                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The design:                                                                               │
│                          │ 1. Keep the efficient initialization (RY shared pairs, RZ pre-rotations) from prior work  │
│                          │ 2. Expand entanglement with linear chain CZ + strategic skip-link CZs (no parameters)     │
│                          │ 3. Use single shared parametrized layer (CRZ reverse) instead of multiple layers          │
│                          │ 4. Restore efficient post-rotation structure (RZ shared pairs only)                       │
│                          │ 5. Removes the expensive global mixing RX/RY layer                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This balances expressivity (via topology) with parameter efficiency, targeting faster     │
│                          │ convergence and reduced train-test gap.                                                   │
