│                          │ CRZ gates. The current program regressed to 0.87 by using a sparse topology. This edit    │
│                          │ proposes implementing the expert recommendation to hybridize the forward entanglement     │
│                          │ block by replacing every other CZ with parametrized CRZ gates.                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This approach:                                                                            │
│                          │ 1. Restores the linear chain topology that proved effective                               │
│                          │ 2. Adds light parameterization to the forward pass with shared "crz_fwd" parameter        │
│                          │ 3. Maintains the reverse shared CRZ pattern that contributed to the 0.91 score            │
│                          │ 4. Keeps parameter count reasonable while improving expressivity                          │
│                          │ 5. Should reduce convergence steps and improve validation loss                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The rationale is that minimal tunable two-qubit rotations during the forward pass can     │
│                          │ enhance expressivity without excessive parameterization overhead, mirroring the           │
│                          │ efficiency gains from the reverse shared CRZ.                                             │
