╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ hybridize_forward_entanglement                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ Analysis of prior programs shows:                                                         │
│                          │ 1. Program 2 (score 0.91) performs best with only 44 parameters, achieving 92% validation │
│                          │ accuracy with excellent efficiency and faster convergence (180 steps).                    │
│                          │ 2. The current program (score 0.90) has regressed to 62 parameters and 270 convergence    │
│                          │ steps, while maintaining only 90% validation accuracy.                                    │
│                          │ 3. The key difference: Program 2 uses a pure CZ forward chain, then a shared-parameter    │
│                          │ CRZ reverse chain. The current program adds a CRY bridge and extra RX/RY global mixing    │
│                          │ layers that increase complexity without improving performance.                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The recommendation to "hybridize the forward entanglement block by replacing every other  │
│                          │ CZ with a shared-parameter CRZ gate" directly aligns with Program 2's successful pattern, │
│                          │ but takes it further: instead of pure CZ gates, we'll alternate CZ and CRZ in the forward │
│                          │ pass. This provides:                                                                      │
│                          │ - Minimal parameter overhead (1 additional parameter for crz_fwd vs pure CZ)              │
│                          │ - Light tuning of forward entanglement to complement the reverse CRZ chain                │
│                          │ - Better parameter efficiency than the current approach                                   │
│                          │ - Maintains the proven lean architecture of Program 2                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The strategy:                                                                             │
│                          │ 1. Remove the ineffective CRY bridge (which added parameters without boosting accuracy)   │
│                          │ 2. Remove the global RX/RY mixing layers (expensive and didn't help)                      │
│                          │ 3. Hybridize the forward CZ chain: CZ, CRZ, CZ, CRZ, CZ, CRZ, CZ pattern                  │
│                          │ 4. Keep the rest of Program 2's lean structure                                            │
│                          │ 5. Expected outcome: ~50-52 parameters, better accuracy, faster convergence, and improved │
│                          │ parameter efficiency                                                                      │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0153                                                                                   │
