                         Patch Metadata - Gen 30/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ skip_link_cz_augmentation                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The current program (score 0.87) has good convergence speed (150 steps) but suffers from  │
│                          │ lower validation accuracy (0.87) and a larger generalization gap (0.04) compared to the   │
│                          │ prior best program (score 0.91, validation 0.92, gap 0.01). The issue appears to be that  │
│                          │ the skip-link topology (step-2 connections) combined with local nearest-neighbor          │
│                          │ connections lacks sufficient long-range entanglement depth.                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The recommendation suggests augmenting the zero-cost CZ chain with extra skip-link CZs    │
│                          │ between specific qubit pairs (0–2, 2–4, 4–6, 6–0) to broaden connectivity at no parameter │
│                          │ cost. However, the current approach already has these skip-links but without the critical │
│                          │ wrap-around connection (6–0).                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key improvements:                                                                     │
│                          │ 1. Add the wrap-around CZ(6,0) to create a circular topology that improves long-range     │
│                          │ correlations                                                                              │
│                          │ 2. Revert to the more parameter-efficient alternating parameter sharing (ry_a/ry_b        │
│                          │ pattern) proven in prior run (score 0.91)                                                 │
│                          │ 3. Keep the reverse chain CRZ for bi-directional information flow from the best prior     │
│                          │ program                                                                                   │
│                          │ 4. Reduce overall parameter count by using simpler shared patterns                        │
│                          │ 5. Maintain the linear chain structure that empirically works best                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This hybrid approach combines:                                                            │
│                          │ - The proven efficient parameter sharing from the 0.91 program                            │
│                          │ - Enhanced connectivity with the wrap-around link from the recommendation                 │
│                          │ - Strategic use of both forward and reverse entanglement chains                           │
│                          │ - Reduced depth and parameter count while maintaining expressivity                        │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0147                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
