                         Patch Metadata - Gen 31/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ hybrid_efficient_expressivity                                                             │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover combines the best aspects of three candidates:                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **From the best prior (0.91 score)**: The lean 44-parameter structure with efficient   │
│                          │ parameter sharing (ry_a/b, rz_pre_a/b, rz_post_a/b) and minimal depth (154), which        │
│                          │ achieves faster convergence (180 steps) and excellent generalization.                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **From the 0.90 inspiration program**: The mid-circuit RX layer for enhanced           │
│                          │ expressivity without adding parameters (all 8 qubits share one parameter). This global    │
│                          │ X-mixing layer provides additional basis rotation capability.                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **From the current program (0.89)**: Removes the skip-link CZ gates which appear to    │
│                          │ have reduced performance (validation accuracy dropped from 0.92 to 0.89), suggesting they │
│                          │ add noise without benefit.                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The strategy is to take the high-efficiency foundation (44 params, good accuracy) and     │
│                          │ selectively add the proven RX rotation layer for improved expressivity. This maintains    │
│                          │ the parameter efficiency that enables fast convergence while gaining the representational │
│                          │ power that helped achieve 0.94 train accuracy in the inspiration program. The RX layer    │
│                          │ acts as a global mixer between the pre-entanglement preparation and post-entanglement     │
│                          │ refinement stages.                                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected improvements:                                                                    │
│                          │ - Validation accuracy: 0.92 (from inspiration program's RX layer)                         │
│                          │ - Parameter efficiency: Maintained at 44 params                                           │
│                          │ - Faster convergence: ~200 steps (between 180 and 300)                                    │
│                          │ - Reduced generalization gap through balanced architecture                                │
