│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key insight is to add a mid-circuit RZ stage between the fixed CZ entanglement and    │
│                          │ the reverse CRY gates. This three-stage RZ sandwich (pre-, mid-, post-entanglement)       │
│                          │ provides:                                                                                 │
│                          │ 1. Enhanced phase flexibility without adding depth                                        │
│                          │ 2. Better separation of concerns: pre-RZ for initialization, mid-RZ for phase adjustment  │
│                          │ after CZ, post-RZ for final rotation                                                      │
│                          │ 3. Only +2 parameters (rz_mid_a, rz_mid_b) for significant expressivity gain              │
│                          │ 4. Potential to accelerate convergence by giving the optimizer more granular phase        │
│                          │ control                                                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This directly builds on the confirmed success of the two-stage RZ approach (pre/post)     │
│                          │ shown in the prior program, extending it to three stages.                                 │
