                         Patch Metadata - Gen 35/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ hybrid_crz_forward_minimal_params                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The current program (score 0.90, 68 params) has added too many parameters and gates,      │
│                          │ increasing depth and complexity without meaningful accuracy gains. The best prior         │
│                          │ performer (score 0.91, 50 params) used alternating CRZ in the reverse chain with only 2   │
│                          │ parameters (crz_rev_a, crz_rev_b), achieving better efficiency.                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key insight: The current program's cross-talk CRY layer (4 params) and mid-circuit RX (1  │
│                          │ shared param) add 40% more parameters than the optimal prior design while validation      │
│                          │ accuracy remains at 0.92. The prior program's strength was parameter efficiency (50       │
│                          │ params vs 68) combined with strategic parameter sharing.                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ New approach:                                                                             │
│                          │ 1. Return to the efficient reverse-chain CRZ alternation (crz_rev_a, crz_rev_b) proven to │
│                          │ work well                                                                                 │
│                          │ 2. Add lightly parametrized forward entanglement: replace alternating CZ gates in the     │
│                          │ forward chain with CRZ using a single shared "crz_fwd" parameter on links [1,2], [3,4],   │
│                          │ [5,6], keeping CZ on [0,1], [2,3], [4,5], [6,7]                                           │
│                          │ 3. Eliminate the cross-talk CRY layer and mid-circuit RX layer entirely                   │
│                          │ 4. Reduce post-entanglement RZ to just one pair-shared parameter                          │
│                          │ 5. Target: ~48-50 params with improved expressivity from bidirectional parametrized gates │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This hybrid approach:                                                                     │
│                          │ - Adds minimal trainable parameters (crz_fwd alone)                                       │
│                          │ - Probes whether weak forward gate tuning improves learning                               │
│                          │ - Maintains the proven efficient reverse chain structure                                  │
│                          │ - Reduces depth and gate count vs current program                                         │
│                          │ - Should improve parameter efficiency while maintaining or improving accuracy             │
