│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ crz_rev_trilogy_asymmetry                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The current program uses a single shared CRY parameter for all 7 reverse chain            │
│                          │ connections, which limits expressivity. The recommendation suggests introducing a         │
│                          │ three-parameter cycling scheme for reverse CRZ gates to add controlled asymmetry without  │
│                          │ significantly increasing parameter count.                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Analysis of prior results:                                                                │
│                          │ - Program 1 (68 params, score 0.90): Full expressivity but high parameter overhead        │
│                          │ - Program 2 (50 params, score 0.91): Better efficiency with 2-parameter CRZ alternation,  │
│                          │ achieved best score                                                                       │
│                          │ - Current (44 params, score 0.90): Single CRY parameter is too constrained despite low    │
│                          │ parameter count                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The strategy is to reintroduce CRZ gates (which showed strong performance in Program 2)   │
│                          │ but use a three-parameter cycling pattern (crz_rev_a, crz_rev_b, crz_rev_c) instead of    │
│                          │ two. This gives +1 parameter (51 total) for improved expressivity while maintaining the   │
│                          │ lean architecture.                                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The cycling pattern (a, b, c, a, b, c, a) for the seven reverse links provides:           │
│                          │ 1. Richer phase diversity in reverse-pass information flow                                │
│                          │ 2. Better capacity to learn complex correlations without overfitting                      │
│                          │ 3. Minimal parameter increase compared to 2-parameter alternation                         │
│                          │ 4. Maintains the efficient chain structure that performed well in Program 2               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected improvements:                                                                    │
│                          │ - Validation accuracy: maintain ~0.93 (already strong)                                    │
│                          │ - Test accuracy: increase toward ~0.91+ (reduce test-train gap)                           │
│                          │ - Generalization gap: tighten via better learned asymmetry                                │
│                          │ - Convergence: potentially faster with more expressive reverse gates                      │
