                         Patch Metadata - Gen 38/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ linear_chain_mid_rz_sandwich                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Revert to the proven linear chain topology from prior program 2 (which achieved the best  │
│                          │ prior score of 0.91 with 0.93 validation accuracy) and add a mid-circuit phase layer as   │
│                          │ recommended. The current sparse skip-link topology achieves only 0.87 validation accuracy │
│                          │ despite shallow depth, indicating that depth reduction without expressivity is            │
│                          │ counterproductive.                                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The improvement combines:                                                                 │
│                          │ 1. Restore linear nearest-neighbor CZ chain (0-1-2-3-4-5-6-7) which was effective in      │
│                          │ prior program 2                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. Insert mid-circuit RZ sandwich with two shared parameters on alternating qubit groups: │
│                          │    - "rz_mid_a" on qubits [0,2,4,6]                                                       │
│                          │    - "rz_mid_b" on qubits [1,3,5,7]                                                       │
│                          │ 3. Use the efficient parameter sharing from prior program 2 (rz_pre_a/b, rz_post_a/b,     │
│                          │ alternating CRZ)                                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This adds only 8 gates and 2 parameters (total ~52 params) while providing three-stage RZ │
│                          │ phase flexibility. The linear chain provides better information flow than skip-links, and │
│                          │ the mid-circuit layer gives the circuit additional expressivity to model the problem      │
│                          │ better.                                                                                   │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0207                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
│ model_name               │ openrouter/anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5                                                     │
│ temperature              │ 1.0                                                                                       │
│ max_output_tokens        │ 16384                                                                                     │
│ diff_summary             │ added: 12; deleted: 0; modified: 35;                                                      │
