│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ three_param_reverse_chain                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The current program (56 params, score 0.90) achieves good test accuracy (0.92) but shows  │
│                          │ a larger generalization gap (0.04) than prior programs (0.02). The prior best program     │
│                          │ used 50 params with a 0.91 score and better generalization.                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key observations:                                                                         │
│                          │ 1. Current program has 7 CRZ reverse gates but only 2 parameters (crz_rev_a, crz_rev_b),  │
│                          │ creating rigid parameter sharing.                                                         │
│                          │ 2. Prior program 2 used 50 params with better balance and faster convergence (330 steps   │
│                          │ but better metric quality).                                                               │
│                          │ 3. The recommendation suggests cycling three shared parameters (crz_rev_a, crz_rev_b,     │
│                          │ crz_rev_c) in the reverse chain to add subtle variety without excessive parameter growth. │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ New approach:                                                                             │
│                          │ - Keep the minimal 2-parameter RY/RZ initialization and post-layers (proven effective).   │
│                          │ - Replace the 2-parameter reverse CRZ chain with a **3-parameter cycling scheme**         │
│                          │ (crz_rev_a → crz_rev_b → crz_rev_c → crz_rev_a → ...).                                    │
│                          │ - Remove the global RX layer (adds parameters without clear benefit; current program uses │
│                          │ it heavily but shows worse generalization).                                               │
│                          │ - Add a **mid-circuit RZ sandwich** (2 parameters) on alternating qubits, matching prior  │
│                          │ best program structure.                                                                   │
│                          │ - This yields ~50-51 params with richer entanglement dynamics, tighter generalization     │
│                          │ gap, and faster convergence.                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Expected improvements:                                                                    │
│                          │ - Reduce generalization gap from 0.04 to ≤0.02                                            │
│                          │ - Maintain or improve test accuracy                                                       │
│                          │ - Converge faster (120→150 steps)                                                         │
│                          │ - Return to ~50 param regime for efficiency                                               │
