│ patch_description        │ This crossover combines the best aspects of both approaches:                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **From the inspiration program (score 0.91, n_params=50)**:                            │
│                          │    - Lean parameter efficiency with only 50 parameters                                    │
│                          │    - Proven alternating CRZ parameter pattern (crz_rev_a/crz_rev_b) that achieves better  │
│                          │ convergence                                                                               │
│                          │    - Simpler structure with fewer layers leads to faster convergence (330 steps vs 300)   │
│                          │    - Best validation accuracy (0.93) and lowest test loss (0.40)                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **From current program (score 0.90, n_params=68)**:                                    │
│                          │    - The CRY cross-talk layer provides long-range correlations between even/odd qubit     │
│                          │ chains                                                                                    │
│                          │    - Mid-circuit RX rotation for additional mixing before final rotations                 │
│                          │    - Better test accuracy (0.92 vs 0.90) suggesting improved generalization               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Optimization Strategy**:                                                             │
│                          │    - Remove redundant Layer 8 (final RY with single shared param) - this is less          │
│                          │ effective than the dual-parameter final RZ scheme                                         │
│                          │    - Keep the efficient alternating CRZ pattern (crz_rev_a/crz_rev_b) instead of single   │
│                          │ crz_back parameter                                                                        │
│                          │    - Preserve the CRY cross-talk connections for long-range entanglement                  │
│                          │    - Add a single mid-circuit RX for mixing (efficient at 1 parameter)                    │
│                          │    - Reduce overall depth while maintaining expressivity                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This hybrid keeps the most efficient parameter sharing from the inspiration program       │
│                          │ (50-60 params range) while incorporating strategic cross-talk connections and mid-circuit │
│                          │ rotation that improve test accuracy and generalization.                                   │
