                         Patch Metadata - Gen 45/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ hybrid_mid_circuit_rz_sandwich                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover combines the best elements from both high-performing programs (score 0.91) │
│                          │ while removing the underperforming global mixing layer from the current program (score    │
│                          │ 0.90).                                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key observations:                                                                         │
│                          │ 1. Both prior programs (score 0.91) achieve validation accuracy of 0.93 and test accuracy │
│                          │ of 0.90, outperforming the current program (0.90 and 0.89 respectively).                  │
│                          │ 2. The first prior program includes a "mid-circuit RZ sandwich" (rz_mid_a and rz_mid_b on │
│                          │ alternating qubits) that provides enhanced phase flexibility - this is NOT present in the │
│                          │ current program.                                                                          │
│                          │ 3. The first prior program uses alternating CRZ parameters (crz_rev_a and crz_rev_b)      │
│                          │ which provides better expressivity than the current program's single shared crz_rev       │
│                          │ parameter.                                                                                │
│                          │ 4. The current program adds CRY bridge gates and excessive global mixing (RX and RY on    │
│                          │ all qubits with shared parameters), which increases parameters to 62 but actually REDUCES │
│                          │ performance compared to prior programs.                                                   │
│                          │ 5. The second prior program achieves 0.91 score with only 50 parameters and slightly      │
│                          │ faster convergence (330 vs 150, but achieving better accuracy).                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Strategy:                                                                                 │
│                          │ - Adopt the proven mid-circuit RZ sandwich architecture from the first prior program      │
│                          │ (adds phase flexibility)                                                                  │
│                          │ - Use alternating CRZ parameters for better control                                       │
│                          │ - Remove the underperforming global mixing layer (RX and RY global)                       │
│                          │ - Remove the ineffective CRY bridge gates                                                 │
│                          │ - Keep the core structure: initial RY, pre-entanglement RZ, linear chain CZ, then         │
│                          │ enhanced parametrized reverse chain, post-entanglement RZ                                 │
│                          │ - This should achieve validation accuracy of 0.93 like the prior programs while           │
│                          │ maintaining good parameter efficiency                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The result should reach 0.91+ combined score with improved validation accuracy (0.93)     │
│                          │ while maintaining reasonable parameter count and convergence speed.                       │
