                         Patch Metadata - Gen 45/80 - Novelty: 2/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ initial_rz_sandwich_chain                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The current program scores 0.87, significantly lower than the prior best (0.91). Analysis │
│                          │ of the prior programs reveals:                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Prior Program 1 (score 0.91)**: Uses alternating parameter sharing (ry_a, ry_b pairs │
│                          │ across all qubits), linear chain CZ entanglement, a mid-circuit RZ sandwich, and reverse  │
│                          │ chain CRZ gates with 62 parameters.                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Prior Program 2 (score 0.91)**: Similar structure but without the mid-circuit RZ     │
│                          │ sandwich, using only 50 parameters with better convergence (330 steps).                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Current Program (score 0.87)**: Uses 4-way parameter grouping (ry_a, ry_b, ry_c,     │
│                          │ ry_d) with sparse diagonal skip-link topology and only nearest-neighbor chains. This      │
│                          │ reduced connectivity and increased parameter count (74 params) hurt performance.          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Key observations**:                                                                     │
│                          │ - The alternating pair-based sharing (ry_a on qubits 0,2,4,6 + ry_b on 1,3,5,7)           │
│                          │ significantly outperforms 4-way grouping                                                  │
│                          │ - Linear chain CZ entanglement with full connectivity is superior to sparse skip-link     │
│                          │ topology                                                                                  │
│                          │ - The mid-circuit RZ sandwich in Program 1 provides +0.04 accuracy boost with minimal     │
│                          │ parameter cost (62 vs 50 params)                                                          │
│                          │ - Parameter efficiency matters: fewer well-chosen parameters converge faster              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Proposed solution**:                                                                    │
│                          │ Adopt the proven structure from Prior Program 1 (which achieved 0.91) but implement the   │
│                          │ recommendation for an initial RZ block to seed the optimization landscape. This adds      │
│                          │ early phase flexibility:                                                                  │
│                          │ - Keep the alternating pair-based RY sharing                                              │
│                          │ - Restore the linear chain CZ topology                                                    │
│                          │ - Add initial RZ seeding on even/odd qubit groups                                         │
│                          │ - Include the mid-circuit RZ sandwich for enhanced phase control                          │
│                          │ - Use the proven reverse chain CRZ pattern                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This combines the best practices: parameter-efficient alternating sharing, proven         │
│                          │ linear-chain entanglement, and layered phase control through initial + mid + post RZ      │
│                          │ blocks.                                                                                   │
