                         Patch Metadata - Gen 48/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ adaptive_phase_fusion                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Inspired by the previous programs' success with parameter sharing and linear chain        │
│                          │ topologies, I identified key patterns:                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **From prior programs**: Linear chain CZ entanglement (0-1-2-3-4-5-6-7) consistently   │
│                          │ delivers ~0.91 score with good parameter efficiency.                                      │
│                          │ 2. **Current program weakness**: Score dropped to 0.90 despite 62 parameters and longer   │
│                          │ convergence (450 steps vs 150-330), suggesting overfitting or inefficient parameter       │
│                          │ utilization. The mixed CRZ/CRX reverse chain may introduce spectral noise without         │
│                          │ sufficient benefit.                                                                       │
│                          │ 3. **Novel insight**: Instead of separate rz_post_a/rz_post_b parameters (16 gates, 2     │
│                          │ parameters), reuse rz_pre_a/rz_pre_b for the final layer. This creates a "fusion" point   │
│                          │ where pre- and post-rotation logic share parameters, reducing total unique parameters     │
│                          │ while testing whether a tighter 2-parameter phase sandwich still captures essential       │
│                          │ dynamics.                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Key differences from prior work**:                                                      │
│                          │ - Eliminate mixed CRZ/CRX and return to pure CRZ reverse chain (better learned pattern    │
│                          │ from prior programs at 50-62 parameters)                                                  │
│                          │ - Merge pre/post RZ phases by reusing rz_pre_a and rz_pre_b at the end                    │
│                          │ - Reduce parameter count from 62 to 54, improving efficiency and convergence speed        │
│                          │ - Maintain proven linear chain CZ topology                                                │
│                          │ - Simplify mid-circuit phase by using single unified even/odd split (rz_mid_a/rz_mid_b    │
│                          │ instead of rz_mid_even/rz_mid_odd for consistency with binary parameter naming)           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is fundamentally different from prior approaches because it fuses architectural      │
│                          │ stages through parameter reuse rather than eliminating gates, preserving expressivity     │
│                          │ while reducing overfitting risk.                                                          │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
