│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ restore_alternating_crz_with_midcircuit_rz                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The current program oversimplified by using a unified CRZ parameter, which reduced        │
│                          │ accuracy to 0.88. Program 1 and 2 both achieved 0.91 by using alternating CRZ parameters  │
│                          │ (crz_rev_a, crz_rev_b). This change:                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Restores alternating CRZ parameters on the reverse chain (crz_rev_a for odd indices,   │
│                          │ crz_rev_b for even indices), matching the proven pattern from Program 2                   │
│                          │ 2. Adds a mid-circuit RZ sandwich immediately after the forward CZ chain, reusing the     │
│                          │ existing rz_phase_a and rz_phase_b parameters on alternating qubits to add phase          │
│                          │ flexibility without new parameter overhead                                                │
│                          │ 3. This recovers the expressivity that was lost in over-simplification while maintaining  │
│                          │ reasonable parameter efficiency (~50 params)                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The goal is to recover the 0.91 score while maintaining the parameter efficiency gains.   │
