│ patch_name               │ restore_crz_add_mid_phase                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The current program replaced parametrized CRZ gates with fixed CZ gates and added RY      │
│                          │ reuse, which degraded performance from 0.91 to 0.87. The prior high-scoring programs      │
│                          │ (0.91) used parametrized CRZ in the reverse chain for enhanced expressivity.              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit restores the proven CRZ reverse chain and adds a mid-circuit RZ phase           │
│                          │ flexibility stage immediately after the forward CZ chain by reusing the existing          │
│                          │ "rz_pre_a" and "rz_pre_b" parameters. This provides extra phase control without adding    │
│                          │ new parameters, bridging the expressivity gap without the computational cost of entirely  │
│                          │ new parameters.                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The RY reuse at the end is removed as it appears to create redundancy rather than         │
│                          │ meaningful additional expressivity.                                                       │
