│ patch_description        │ This crossover combines the best elements from three candidate implementations:           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **From Current Program (score 0.90)**: The fast convergence (120 steps) and parameter  │
│                          │ efficiency (56 params) with minimal depth (123), plus the global RX layer which enhances  │
│                          │ Hilbert-space mixing.                                                                     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **From Prior Program 2 (score 0.91)**: The cleaner 50-parameter architecture without   │
│                          │ initial RZ seeding, which achieves better parameter efficiency and similar validation     │
│                          │ accuracy (0.93).                                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **From Prior Program 1 (score 0.91)**: The alternating RZ mid-circuit layers           │
│                          │ (rz_mid_a/b) that provide enhanced phase flexibility without excessive parameter growth.  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Key Design Choices**:                                                                   │
│                          │ - Remove the redundant initial RZ seeding block (rz_init_a/b) that adds 16 gates but      │
│                          │ doesn't improve performance                                                               │
│                          │ - Keep the minimal 2-parameter sharing scheme for RY and RZ layers (ry_a/b, rz_pre_a/b,   │
│                          │ rz_post_a/b)                                                                              │
│                          │ - Include the mid-circuit RZ sandwich with alternating qubit groups (rz_mid_a/b) for      │
│                          │ phase flexibility                                                                         │
│                          │ - Maintain the standard forward linear chain CZ gates                                     │
│                          │ - Use the split CRZ reverse chain (crz_rev_a for odd, crz_rev_b for even indices)         │
│                          │ - Remove the global RX layer from current program (adds 8 gates and parameters without    │
│                          │ clear benefit based on validation metrics)                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ **Expected Improvements**:                                                                │
│                          │ - Validation accuracy: maintain 0.93 (best from both priors)                              │
│                          │ - Parameter count: ~66 (between 50 and 74, with added mid-circuit RZ)                     │
│                          │ - Convergence speed: retain fast convergence from current program                         │
│                          │ - Generalization gap: improve from 0.04 to ~0.02 by balancing expressivity and parameter  │
│                          │ sharing                                                                                   │
│                          │ - Combined score: target 0.91+                                                            │
