╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ merge_rz_phases_for_efficiency                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ Analysis of the prior programs shows that the best performer (0.91 combined score) uses   │
│                          │ only 50 parameters with a simple two-parameter phase schedule (rz_pre_a/rz_pre_b) in both │
│                          │ pre- and post-entanglement positions. The current program has 62 parameters and scores    │
│                          │ 0.90, indicating parameter bloat is hurting generalization.                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The recommendation is to merge the post-entanglement RZ rotations to reuse the            │
│                          │ pre-entanglement parameters. This reduces the parameter count from 62 to 54 while         │
│                          │ preserving the proven two-stage structure. The hypothesis is that:                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. The pre-entanglement phase conditioning and post-entanglement phase conditioning serve │
│                          │ similar roles in a single ansatz block                                                    │
│                          │ 2. Reusing parameters reduces overfitting and improves parameter efficiency               │
│                          │ 3. The model can still learn effectively by optimizing shared phases across both stages   │
│                          │ 4. This brings us closer to the 50-parameter sweet spot of the best prior performer       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This targeted change tests whether the current circuit's spectral diversity (mixing CRZ   │
