│ patch_name               │ hybrid_crx_cz_linear_chain                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves good parameter efficiency (50 params) but suffers from lower │
│                          │ accuracy (0.87 validation) compared to the prior programs (0.93). The prior programs used │
│                          │ a linear chain topology with parametrized controlled gates (CRZ) in the reverse           │
│                          │ direction, achieving superior results.                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key insights from context programs:                                                       │
│                          │ 1. Linear chain CZ entanglement (0→1→2→...→7) is highly effective for this problem        │
│                          │ 2. Parametrized controlled gates (CRZ with alternating parameters) add significant        │
│                          │ expressivity                                                                              │
│                          │ 3. Alternating parameter sharing on single-qubit rotations (odd/even qubits) is efficient │
│                          │ 4. The combination of forward CZ chain + reverse parametrized chain works best            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current program's weakness is the sparse skip-link topology with independent 2-qubit  │
│                          │ parameter groups, which lacks the strong connectivity of the linear chain.                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Novel approach: Combine insights by:                                                      │
│                          │ 1. Restore the proven linear chain CZ topology for forward entanglement                   │
│                          │ 2. Replace the sparse topology with a hybrid: use CRZ gates in reverse chain (like prior  │
│                          │ programs) but strategically use CRX on the most central qubits to test axis diversity     │
│                          │ 3. Use aggressive parameter sharing with odd/even alternation (4 parameters total for     │
│                          │ single-qubit gates)                                                                       │
│                          │ 4. Maintain minimal but effective depth while preserving the expressivity of parametrized │
│                          │ two-qubit gates                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This hybrid approach respects the validated linear chain structure while introducing      │
│                          │ controlled axis variation through CRX on central qubits, balancing exploration with       │
│                          │ exploitation of known good patterns.                                                      │
