│ patch_description        │ The current program's added rx_global layer increased parameters to 56 and worsened       │
│                          │ generalization (gap 0.04 vs 0.02). The prior best programs achieved 0.91 combined score   │
│                          │ with exactly 50 parameters using only two-parameter phase schedules (rz_pre_a, rz_pre_b). │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit:                                                                                │
│                          │ 1. Removes the 8-qubit rx_global layer entirely (saves 8 gate instances, reduces          │
│                          │ parameter bloat)                                                                          │
│                          │ 2. Merges post-entanglement RZ rotations to reuse rz_pre_a/rz_pre_b instead of            │
│                          │ rz_post_a/rz_post_b (reduces unique parameters from 10 to 8 for phase layers)             │
│                          │ 3. Returns to the proven 50-parameter configuration while keeping the efficient linear    │
│                          │ chain entanglement                                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This should recover the 0.91 combined score by reducing overfitting and improving         │
│                          │ parameter efficiency, while maintaining the validated entanglement structure.             │
