│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ restore_alternating_crz_remove_global_mixing                                              │
│ patch_description        │ The current program introduced a global RX/RY mixing layer and over-simplified the        │
│                          │ reverse CRZ chain to a single shared parameter. Analysis of prior high-performing         │
│                          │ programs shows:                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. The alternating CRZ parameter pattern (crz_rev_a and crz_rev_b) achieved validation    │
│                          │ accuracy of 0.93 and combined score 0.91 with only 50 parameters                          │
│                          │ 2. The current fully-shared CRZ reverse chain (single "crz_rev" param) reduced validation │
│                          │ accuracy to 0.90 and increased parameters to 62                                           │
│                          │ 3. The global RX/RY mixing layer (16 gates, 2 shared params) does not compensate—it adds  │
│                          │ bulk without sufficient expressivity                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit restores the proven alternating CRZ pattern and removes the ineffective global  │
│                          │ mixing layer. This reduces parameter count, improves parameter efficiency, and recovers   │
│                          │ the expressivity that prior programs achieved. The parameter efficiency metric confirms   │
│                          │ that fewer, better-utilized parameters are preferable to bulk parameters with poor        │
│                          │ sharing.                                                                                  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0182                                                                                   │
