│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ restore_linear_chain_with_forward_crz                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ The current sparse diagonal skip-link topology underperforms (0.87 vs 0.91) despite       │
│                          │ similar parameter count. The prior programs achieved 0.91 with a proven linear chain CZ   │
│                          │ entanglement topology and parametrized reverse-chain CRZ gates.                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit restores the linear chain structure and extends the reverse-chain CRZ pattern   │
│                          │ into the forward pass by replacing CZ gates on [1,2] and [5,6] with shared parametrized   │
│                          │ CRZ("crz_fwd") gates. This:                                                               │
│                          │ - Restores the proven low-depth linear chain entanglement                                 │
│                          │ - Adds learnable forward-direction coupling (consistent with the recommendation)          │
│                          │ - Maintains 50 parameters while improving expressivity                                    │
│                          │ - Should recover validation accuracy to ~0.93 range                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The change directly implements the proposed recommendation to "swap CZ on wires [1,2] and │
│                          │ [5,6] for CRZ('crz_fwd')" while keeping the proven chain structure.                       │
