                         Patch Metadata - Gen 56/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ lightweight_rzbridge_circuit                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ The current program (score 0.90) uses 68 parameters and has slower convergence (300       │
│                          │ steps). The prior best program (score 0.91) used only 50 parameters with faster           │
│                          │ convergence (180 steps) and better parameter efficiency (0.02 vs 0.01).                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key insight is that the current program over-parameterizes with:                      │
│                          │ - 4 unique RY parameters (ry_init_a, ry_init_b, ry_final, plus the final global one)      │
│                          │ - 3 unique RZ parameters (rz_prep_a, rz_prep_b, rz_final_a, rz_final_b)                   │
│                          │ - Multiple independent CRY and CRX gates across the circuit                               │
│                          │ - A global RX layer that adds 1 more parameter                                            │
│                          │ - Total: 68 parameters                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ To improve, I'll:                                                                         │
│                          │ 1. Simplify the parameter structure back toward the proven 50-parameter design            │
│                          │ 2. Remove the expensive CRY cross-talk layer (Layer 4) which adds 2 parameters            │
│                          │ 3. Use the proven CRZ reverse chain with parameter alternation (crz_rev_a, crz_rev_b)     │
│                          │ 4. Keep the mid-circuit RZ layer after the reverse CRZ chain, reusing rz_prep_a and       │
│                          │ rz_prep_b as suggested                                                                    │
│                          │ 5. Maintain the linear CZ forward chain                                                   │
│                          │ 6. Use only essential RY and RZ rotations with strong parameter sharing                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This reduces parameters to ~44-46, improves parameter efficiency, and should converge     │
│                          │ faster while maintaining or exceeding validation accuracy. The mid-circuit RZ bridge      │
│                          │ (reusing parameters) adds flexibility without increasing unique parameter count.          │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0168                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
