│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ crz_mid_phase_expansion                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ The current program (score 0.87) uses fixed CZ gates in the reverse chain, which limits   │
│                          │ expressivity compared to prior versions that used parametrized CRZ gates (score 0.91).    │
│                          │ The key issue is that the reverse chain has lost learned phase modulation.                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ My new approach restores parametrized control in the reverse chain by:                    │
│                          │ 1. Replacing reverse CZ gates with CRZ gates (reusing crz_rev_a and crz_rev_b alternating │
│                          │ pattern)                                                                                  │
│                          │ 2. Adding a strategic mid-circuit RZ layer immediately after the reverse CRZ chain,       │
│                          │ reusing rz_pre_a and rz_pre_b to add phase flexibility without increasing parameter count │
│                          │ 3. Removing the redundant post-entanglement RY layer (which reuses ry_a, ry_b) to keep    │
│                          │ parameter efficiency high while restoring the proven CRZ structure                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This combines the best of both prior programs:                                            │
│                          │ - Restores the parametrized CRZ reverse chain from Program 1 (which achieved 0.91)        │
│                          │ - Adds an extra lightweight RZ layer for finer phase control                              │
│                          │ - Maintains 50 parameters like Program 1, but with better expressivity through the        │
│                          │ mid-circuit phase adjustment                                                              │
│                          │ - Should reduce the validation loss (currently 0.47, target ~0.33) and improve            │
│                          │ generalization gap                                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The depth increases slightly but the parametrized gates provide better learning capacity, │
│                          │ matching the prior successful pattern.                                                    │
