│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ merged_phase_schedule                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ This redesign merges the pre- and post-entanglement RZ phase schedules into a unified     │
│                          │ parameter set, reducing unique parameters from 50 to 48 while maintaining expressivity.   │
│                          │ The key structural change is replacing all `"rz_post_a"` and `"rz_post_b"` references     │
│                          │ with `"rz_pre_a"` and `"rz_pre_b"` respectively in the final RZ block.                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The rationale is that since both pre and post phases operate on the same even/odd qubit   │
│                          │ pairs, parameter sharing can encode the combined phase rotation more efficiently without  │
│                          │ sacrificing model capacity. This tighter parameter budget should improve generalization,  │
│                          │ reduce overfitting risk, and maintain the high validation accuracy (0.93-0.94) achieved   │
│                          │ in prior runs.                                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Structural improvements:                                                                  │
│                          │ - Unified phase modulation: Pre and post RZ phases now share a two-parameter basis        │
│                          │ (rz_pre_a, rz_pre_b)                                                                      │
│                          │ - Reduced redundancy: Eliminates the unnecessary distinction between rz_post_* and        │
│                          │ rz_pre_*                                                                                  │
│                          │ - Cleaner parameter semantics: Even qubits (0,2,4,6) always use the same parameter        │
│                          │ family; odd qubits (1,3,5,7) use the other                                                │
│                          │ - Expected outcome: Comparable or improved validation accuracy with 4% fewer parameters   │
│                          │ and potentially faster convergence                                                        │
