│ patch_name               │ hybrid_crx_core_ansatz                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ This redesign introduces targeted structural improvements to the current high-performing  │
│                          │ ansatz while maintaining its efficient 50-parameter architecture. The key innovation      │
│                          │ replaces the central reverse-chain CRZ gates (on qubits [4,3] and [3,2]) with CRX gates   │
│                          │ using a shared parameter. This strategic substitution:                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Introduces axis diversity**: The current design relies heavily on Z-axis             │
│                          │ entanglement. By injecting X-axis parametrized entanglement at the circuit's core (the    │
│                          │ middle qubits), we add orthogonal expressivity without parameter explosion.               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Maintains efficiency**: Uses only one additional unique parameter (crx_rev_c),       │
│                          │ keeping total parameters at 51—a negligible increase that should not degrade convergence  │
│                          │ speed.                                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 3. **Targets expressivity bottleneck**: The middle qubits (2, 3, 4) are the most          │
│                          │ constrained in a linear chain. CRX gates here can capture rotational symmetries that CRZ  │
│                          │ cannot, potentially improving generalization by reducing the train-test gap.              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 4. **Preserves proven structure**: All other layers (initial RY/RZ, forward CZ chain,     │
│                          │ mid-circuit phases, forward/backward CRZ chain, post-entanglement) remain intact,         │
│                          │ retaining the architecture that achieved 0.91 score.                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This minimal, surgical modification tests whether localized axis variation at the circuit │
│                          │ core improves performance without architectural overhead.                                 │
