                         Patch Metadata - Gen 63/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ merge_rz_post_to_pre                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The current 56-parameter circuit achieves excellent test accuracy (0.92) but has a lower  │
│                          │ combined score (0.90 vs 0.91) than the 50-parameter prior variants. The post-entanglement │
│                          │ RZ layer uses distinct parameters `rz_post_a` and `rz_post_b`, but prior experiments      │
│                          │ showed that reusing `rz_pre_a` and `rz_pre_b` in the mid-circuit layer maintained         │
│                          │ expressivity while reducing parameters.                                                   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit merges the post-entanglement RZ parameters into the pre-entanglement parameters │
│                          │ by replacing:                                                                             │
│                          │ - All `"rz_post_a"` → `"rz_pre_a"`                                                        │
│                          │ - All `"rz_post_b"` → `"rz_pre_b"`                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This reduces the ansatz from 56 to 48 parameters while preserving the circuit structure   │
│                          │ and the strong test generalization (0.92) already achieved. The dual application of phase │
│                          │ parameters at different circuit depths should maintain or enhance expressivity through    │
│                          │ multi-stage phase modulation.                                                             │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0123                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
│ model_name               │ openrouter/anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5                                                     │
│ temperature              │ 1.0                                                                                       │
│ max_output_tokens        │ 16384                                                                                     │
│ diff_summary             │ added: 1; deleted: 0; modified: 9;                                                        │
