│ patch_name               │ restore_linear_crz_chain                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The current sparse diagonal topology with separate even/odd skip connections is           │
│                          │ underperforming (0.87 vs 0.91). The prior successful programs used a complete linear      │
│                          │ chain CZ layer (0-1-2-3-4-5-6-7) followed by reverse chain CRZ parametrized gates,        │
│                          │ achieving 0.91 score with only 50 parameters.                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current approach with sparse connections and missing CRZ reverse chain is less        │
│                          │ effective. By restoring the proven linear chain CZ topology and adding the reverse CRZ    │
│                          │ gates back, we recover the high-connectivity entanglement pattern while keeping parameter │
│                          │ grouping efficient.                                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This targets:                                                                             │
│                          │ - Restoring validation_accuracy from 0.87 to 0.93+                                        │
│                          │ - Reducing the generalization gap from 0.04 to 0.02                                       │
│                          │ - Reducing test_loss from 0.46 to 0.40                                                    │
│                          │ - Keeping parameter count low with strategic sharing                                      │
