│ patch_description        │ The current program added unnecessary parameters (cry_bridge, rx_global, ry_global) that  │
│                          │ degraded performance. The first program achieved 0.91 with only 50 parameters through     │
│                          │ aggressive sharing.                                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit returns to the proven 50-parameter architecture (RY→RZ_pre→CZ chain→CRZ reverse │
│                          │ chain→RZ_post structure) and duplicates the entire multi-stage block to form two          │
│                          │ back-to-back layers that reuse all parameter names. This tests whether increased depth    │
│                          │ (doubled to ~320) with full parameter sharing improves expressivity and convergence       │
│                          │ without increasing the parameter budget beyond 50.                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key differences from current:                                                             │
│                          │ - Removes cry_bridge, rx_global, ry_global (added bloat)                                  │
│                          │ - Returns to CRZ alternation (crz_rev_a/b) instead of full sharing                        │
│                          │ - Duplicates entire block with parameter name reuse                                       │
│                          │ - Maintains 50-parameter budget (2 layers × 25 unique params per layer with full sharing) │
