                         Patch Metadata - Gen 71/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ deep_param_shared_dual_stage                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ Analysis of current metrics shows:                                                        │
│                          │ - Current: validation_acc=0.92, test_acc=0.90, convergence=330 steps, depth=154           │
│                          │ - Prior best: validation_acc=0.94, test_acc=0.89, convergence=180 steps, depth=160        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key observations:                                                                         │
│                          │ 1. Current design has 50 params but slower convergence (330 vs 180 steps) and lower       │
│                          │ validation accuracy (0.92 vs 0.94)                                                        │
│                          │ 2. The generalization gap is 0.03 (high), indicating overfitting despite good training    │
│                          │ accuracy                                                                                  │
│                          │ 3. Prior designs achieved faster convergence by using parameter reuse more aggressively   │
│                          │ (fused pre/post RZ layers)                                                                │
│                          │ 4. Depth=154 is lower than optimal (160), suggesting insufficient expressivity            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ New approach:                                                                             │
│                          │ - Reintroduce the proven fused RZ layer pattern (rz_pre_a/rz_pre_b reused as mid-circuit  │
│                          │ layer) which gave validation_acc=0.94                                                     │
│                          │ - Add a second stage of controlled rotations using CRX instead of just CRZ to increase    │
│                          │ expressivity without adding parameters                                                    │
│                          │ - Use deeper parameter sharing to maintain 50-param budget while increasing effective     │
│                          │ capacity                                                                                  │
│                          │ - Organize as two sub-blocks: (1) RY→RZ_pre→CZ→mid-RZ, (2) CRX forward→CRZ                │
│                          │ reverse→RZ_post                                                                           │
│                          │ - This balances expressivity (mixed CRX/CRZ), convergence speed (parameter reuse), and    │
│                          │ validation performance                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
