│ patch_description        │ Add a wrap-around CZ + CRZ gate pair connecting qubit 7 to qubit 0, implementing          │
│                          │ ring-topology long-range coupling. This single additional parameter (crz_wrap) tests      │
│                          │ whether ring-based entanglement improves the validation-test generalization gap without   │
│                          │ significantly increasing circuit depth or parameter count.                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The prior programs achieved validation accuracy of 0.93-0.94 but test accuracy of         │
│                          │ 0.89-0.90. The current program improved test accuracy to 0.91 but validation dropped to   │
│                          │ 0.92, reducing combined score to 0.90. Adding ring-topology coupling may help bridge this │
│                          │ gap by enabling information flow across the full qubit register, potentially improving    │
│                          │ both validation accuracy and generalization.                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This is a low-risk, parameter-efficient modification that leverages the natural ring      │
│                          │ structure of an 8-qubit system.                                                           │
