│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_wrap_around_crz                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ Add a wrap-around CZ gate followed by a parametrized CRZ gate connecting the last qubit   │
│                          │ (7) back to the first qubit (0). This creates a ring topology instead of a linear chain,  │
│                          │ enabling:                                                                                 │
│                          │ 1. Long-range information flow between boundary qubits                                    │
│                          │ 2. Better generalization through improved quantum entanglement structure                  │
│                          │ 3. Potential faster convergence via enhanced connectivity                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This single new parameter (crz_wrap) leverages the proven CRZ effectiveness from the      │
│                          │ reverse chain section while testing ring-topology benefits on generalization gap          │
│                          │ (currently 0.03, target ≤0.02). The minimal gate overhead is justified by addressing the  │
│                          │ convergence slowdown (330 vs 180 steps in prior runs) through structural improvements.    │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
